Mandatory Sustainability Reporting: Starting January 2025, Main Board issuers must comply with the new climate-related disclosure requirements based on ISSB standards (IFRS S2) on a "comply or explain" basis. Large Cap Issuers must adopt these disclosures mandatorily by January 2026, with broader implementation for Publicly Accountable Entities (PAEs) by 2028.

Governance and Assurance: The roadmap introduces a phased approach to mandatory assurance for sustainability disclosures and establishes a comprehensive governance structure involving the Hong Kong Institute of Certified Public Accountants (HKICPA) and the Accounting and Financial Reporting Council (AFRC).

Capacity Building: A focus on improving skills, technology, and data to support high-quality disclosures, including initiatives like the Hong Kong Green Fintech Map and local assurance standards.

The roadmap emphasizes alignment with international practices while addressing Hong Kong’s specific economic and market conditions. It aims to attract global investment by enhancing trust in sustainability reporting.', 'The Roadmap on Sustainability Disclosure in Hong Kong, published in December 2024, outlines Hong Kong’s strategy to adopt and implement sustainability disclosure standards aligned with the International Sustainability Standards Board (ISSB). This roadmap aims to strengthen the transparency, consistency, and quality of sustainability-related financial disclosures in Hong Kong. Key milestones include:

Mandatory Sustainability Reporting: Starting January 2025, Main Board issuers must comply with the new climate-related disclosure requirements based on ISSB standards (IFRS S2) on a "comply or explain" basis. Large Cap Issuers must adopt these disclosures mandatorily by January 2026, with broader implementation for Publicly Accountable Entities (PAEs) by 2028.

Governance and Assurance: The roadmap introduces a phased approach to mandatory assurance for sustainability disclosures and establishes a comprehensive governance structure involving the Hong Kong Institute of Certified Public Accountants (HKICPA) and the Accounting and Financial Reporting Council (AFRC).

Capacity Building: A focus on improving skills, technology, and data to support high-quality disclosures, including initiatives like the Hong Kong Green Fintech Map and local assurance standards.

The roadmap emphasizes alignment with international practices while addressing Hong Kong’s specific economic and market conditions. It aims to attract global investment by enhancing trust in sustainability reporting.', 'The Roadmap on Sustainability Disclosure in Hong Kong, published in December 2024, outlines Hong Kong’s strategy to adopt and implement sustainability disclosure standards aligned with the International Sustainability Standards Board (ISSB). This roadmap aims to strengthen the transparency, consistency, and quality of sustainability-related financial disclosures in Hong Kong. Key milestones include:

